%% End-to-end walk-through of note1.txt through the pipeline.
%% Source ASCII: EXTRACTOR_EXPLAINED.md section 8.
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant CLI as cli.py
    participant Pipe as pipeline.py
    participant Ingest as ingest.py
    participant Model as model.py
    participant Extract as extract.py
    participant Clean as cleanup.py
    participant Disk as outputs/

    User->>CLI: python -m extractor.cli --input samples
    CLI->>Pipe: extract_from_file(llm, note1.txt)
    Pipe->>Ingest: read_document(path)
    Ingest-->>Pipe: ~700 chars of text
    Pipe->>Ingest: chunk_text(text)
    Ingest-->>Pipe: 1 chunk (fits in n_ctx)
    Note over Model: model already loaded (~3s first time)
    Pipe->>Extract: extract_json(llm, chunk)
    Extract->>Model: create_chat_completion (grammar-constrained)
    Model-->>Extract: schema-valid JSON
    Extract-->>Pipe: patient, diagnoses, medications
    Pipe->>Ingest: merge_extractions([json])
    Ingest-->>Pipe: same dict (only one chunk)
    Pipe->>Clean: clean_extraction(dict)
    Clean-->>Pipe: ISO dates, merged dx, stripped doses
    Pipe->>Disk: write note1.json + summary.csv row
